                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "60387ce2-5911-49ec-a42c-7b831b753f6c",
                        "entry_id": "7ea1cba7-7248-3b8e-811d-98d2fb9e0b26",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more frickle"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "e721f032-9996-476e-8959-4ccf5ca1e97b",
                        "entry_id": "7ea1cba7-7248-3b8e-811d-98d2fb9e0b26",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most frickle"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bb5c5ef4-833b-33e4-8d4f-75e028f70427",
                        "entry_id": "7ea1cba7-7248-3b8e-811d-98d2fb9e0b26",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Not solid or firm; loose; friable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0fb6af38-ff0c-4c01-b24a-d35d89d84192",
                                "sense_id": "bb5c5ef4-833b-33e4-8d4f-75e028f70427",
                                "text": "Vpon this fain and frickle foundation of two false and contrary opinions was that leage of Smalcaldium stroken: whereof ensued that lamentable and cruell warre, to the greate waste and destruction of Germany, with the murder of infinit thousands of men."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f9a5352-ee21-42fe-a3cc-ef16561fc358",
                                "sense_id": "bb5c5ef4-833b-33e4-8d4f-75e028f70427",
                                "text": "it is extremely frickle in the limestone formation;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "536c5390-d0f7-4386-a9c1-512de51d7920",
                                "sense_id": "bb5c5ef4-833b-33e4-8d4f-75e028f70427",
                                "text": "The land which is kept loose and frickle offers opportunity for the plants to grow — then it prevents evaporation and the moisture is stored up for the plants use when the dry season comes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "444bccc0-7c6f-36e5-b5e7-163733c2f620",
                        "entry_id": "7ea1cba7-7248-3b8e-811d-98d2fb9e0b26",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Changeable; undependable; fickle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "87cd3508-9e6e-42e1-a7c8-b8f2fa04173d",
                                "sense_id": "444bccc0-7c6f-36e5-b5e7-163733c2f620",
                                "text": "Yvette Guilbert, a greater favourite than ever with the generally frickle and changeable Parisians, has been singing for three nights at Lyons, where she received 1000 francs an evening—that is, ₤40."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ee1b3c0-4966-4951-b07f-367b99d10d31",
                                "sense_id": "444bccc0-7c6f-36e5-b5e7-163733c2f620",
                                "text": "And thither Jeanne set out, in March 1557, accompanied by the frickle, wayward, sinning Antoine and the boy who was his living image."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8267b932-523f-4d80-b49d-4f47fdde3aeb",
                                "sense_id": "444bccc0-7c6f-36e5-b5e7-163733c2f620",
                                "text": "And now most of our warriors have forgotten us, and the frickle nation bellows: 'Long live King Absalom!'"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f5dfb5d-ba5a-4094-ae71-d93c863acad4",
                                "sense_id": "444bccc0-7c6f-36e5-b5e7-163733c2f620",
                                "text": "Is the hon. Member also aware that Opposition Members are frickle minded, even though they are not here"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c2fde3c-ad18-4a71-ab20-20d6d7f2f7d4",
                                "sense_id": "444bccc0-7c6f-36e5-b5e7-163733c2f620",
                                "text": "It is perhaps the perfect paradox of contemporary liquid life: all the trends in today’s work-life quite clearly suggest a rapid destabilization of social bonds corresponding with increasingly disempowering effects of a frickle and uncertain global high-tech information economy, yet those workers caught in the epicenter of this bewildering shift express a sense of mastery over their lives, interpreting their professional identity in this context in terms of indvidual-level control and empowering agency (du Gay, 1996; Storey et al, 2005)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c1be4ea-2964-4c9a-b509-42715fc7f0c2",
                                "sense_id": "444bccc0-7c6f-36e5-b5e7-163733c2f620",
                                "text": "It's only because our mind is frickle and so they easily bounce back at times."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2a815a15-daf0-4738-908c-ee31d6a88eaa",
                                "sense_id": "444bccc0-7c6f-36e5-b5e7-163733c2f620",
                                "text": "The making of friends by that man is not certain, who is of an unsteady mind, or who does not serve old men, or who is not constant in his opinions, or who is of a frickle disposition."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "c74eeab0-d39b-3e30-b1fd-82dde3b1c889",
                "word": "frickle",
                "pos": "intj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "aa5caa7a-64eb-3e2e-a850-f1cd35e94a9b",
                        "entry_id": "c74eeab0-d39b-3e30-b1fd-82dde3b1c889",
                        "glosses": [
                            "a minced oath"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3862e860-aa38-422e-941c-170e1c1709d7",
                                "sense_id": "aa5caa7a-64eb-3e2e-a850-f1cd35e94a9b",
                                "text": "\"Frickle frackle,” she said, stomping out."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "085535f0-2744-4528-aea9-ed1fa85044dd",
                                "sense_id": "aa5caa7a-64eb-3e2e-a850-f1cd35e94a9b",
                                "text": "I know that they loved me and all that frickle-feely stuff, surely wanted the best but I didn't care too much for love—at least not now."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f9b42db-dae2-498b-a0a7-e35f03fda13a",
                                "sense_id": "aa5caa7a-64eb-3e2e-a850-f1cd35e94a9b",
                                "text": "Finally, I though of something with survival value: I need to get the frickle out of here before anyone sees this tattoo!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "3dfbe7a2-71d5-3f0d-903c-d1b0b627381c",
                "word": "frickle",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "5e04d640-b2fe-4371-80c8-f692b8dde1de",
