                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "17f92750-97b7-323f-8fef-d04bd4fc4482",
                        "entry_id": "3dfbe7a2-71d5-3f0d-903c-d1b0b627381c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A fried pickle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Canada",
                            "US"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "34dce518-388b-4091-b489-8d2b17200dc9",
                                "sense_id": "17f92750-97b7-323f-8fef-d04bd4fc4482",
                                "text": "Frickles (fried pickles) are inspired and served with a blue cheese dipping sauce (see page 20)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "626306eb-4ba5-46a7-9214-787d8b113fdd",
                                "sense_id": "17f92750-97b7-323f-8fef-d04bd4fc4482",
                                "text": "Raise your hand if you love fried pickies (both my hands are raised). There is no stopping my love for pickle-anything, but frickles take it to a whole new level."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f14f56cd-cbe4-44ec-a0bf-b8449dddbeb8",
                                "sense_id": "17f92750-97b7-323f-8fef-d04bd4fc4482",
                                "text": "Using the deep-fryer's wire basket, a slotted spoon, or a spider, remove the frickles to paper towels to absorb extra oil or drain on a wire rack."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "46558d1e-3a95-3838-a035-2e458cdc58d8",
                "word": "frickle",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "54308eff-a98d-4cba-bc3d-6b1de248c9a8",
                        "entry_id": "46558d1e-3a95-3838-a035-2e458cdc58d8",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "frickles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d6680f1a-1c89-3e0f-87ff-25762773f2ac",
                        "entry_id": "46558d1e-3a95-3838-a035-2e458cdc58d8",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A penis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "euphemistic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4272cc6-f4dd-4b26-b8bd-9dc8bdf104ac",
                                "sense_id": "d6680f1a-1c89-3e0f-87ff-25762773f2ac",
                                "text": "\"A frickle is for a boy and a frackle is for a girl,” Belle explains with a shrug, like it's the most normal thing in the world."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7f26a63f-9d71-4136-bfe2-cde447e352e0",
                                "sense_id": "d6680f1a-1c89-3e0f-87ff-25762773f2ac",
                                "text": "After all, creative positioning during the venereal act (“frickle-frackle!”) can cause fungal growth, cancer, and death."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "48a4d225-0f41-4ab7-9b51-63603e9971bf",
                                "sense_id": "d6680f1a-1c89-3e0f-87ff-25762773f2ac",
                                "text": "But looking at the above, we can start to understand why when we say \"virgin,\" we mean virgin in the sense that we know virgin today—that she didn't do the old frickle-frackle with Joseph."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "82ac2235-db0b-3acd-a07e-69e49c47d002",
                "word": "frickle",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
