                        ],
                        "form": "frickling"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "2d84b379-ebdc-4001-8d3a-e30ffc62c03c",
                        "entry_id": "4f93a128-a525-367b-9f21-a02b9e7409bf",
                        "tags": [
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "frickled"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "476a10ac-aba0-4f18-916d-2c9cd575d9fa",
                        "entry_id": "4f93a128-a525-367b-9f21-a02b9e7409bf",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "frickled"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e7c7c8b1-dd67-346b-9534-93ec1a07fc41",
                        "entry_id": "4f93a128-a525-367b-9f21-a02b9e7409bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To upset or discombobulate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "26ca6a80-510c-4f9a-9b03-0cd1f9a48d7a",
                                "sense_id": "e7c7c8b1-dd67-346b-9534-93ec1a07fc41",
                                "text": "In his own Yorkshire words, they made him 'reet frickled', and any senior officers who came to inspect us never got their messages correctly delivered if poor Thompson was on duty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "04df9f9c-8223-49a0-81fb-6e977a8dea80",
                                "sense_id": "e7c7c8b1-dd67-346b-9534-93ec1a07fc41",
                                "text": "Linda, at the Deli in Anchorage and the Cup in Tucson, has had spirited run-ins with cooks who did not attack their work with the same ferocity she did. Just last Sunday, a Cup cook \"freaked\" and got \"real frickled” when she put up tickets faster than he liked."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2992a623-6d17-4c78-b575-f66d496c084c",
                                "sense_id": "e7c7c8b1-dd67-346b-9534-93ec1a07fc41",
                                "text": "Sometimes the noise changed pitch and made my scales frickle, sounding like the moan of a doomed wooden ship when it runs aground."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4bfdccc-bf8c-45b3-b471-b839ef678ec4",
                                "sense_id": "e7c7c8b1-dd67-346b-9534-93ec1a07fc41",
                                "text": "Meagre flees can't frickle this mad villany"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "844d4ea1-a4e5-3847-a84e-4f2c7b56bb9a",
                        "entry_id": "4f93a128-a525-367b-9f21-a02b9e7409bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To move, act, or change randomly."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7868d681-e1f7-42f5-a47c-253f3cc93a61",
                                "sense_id": "844d4ea1-a4e5-3847-a84e-4f2c7b56bb9a",
                                "text": "The ball took a lucky bounce for JSU and frickled away from the goal before a Panther player could capitalize on the rebound, and the game remained scoreless."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ec6830d-fe57-4de1-abb4-d34436621c3d",
                                "sense_id": "844d4ea1-a4e5-3847-a84e-4f2c7b56bb9a",
                                "text": "I got the porridge going – in the right saucepan mind, while Johnny frickled round my feet and the constant threat of Felix climbing out of his basket, desperate to copy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d49adc94-d21c-44b7-aae9-8aee96d26207",
                                "sense_id": "844d4ea1-a4e5-3847-a84e-4f2c7b56bb9a",
                                "text": "Mood became frickled from sudden smile to very rude."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e8105889-8d47-386f-8510-f82bb4e75a3b",
                        "entry_id": "4f93a128-a525-367b-9f21-a02b9e7409bf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To speckle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f4d0802-a014-4bbd-82db-118d9cc1d568",
                                "sense_id": "e8105889-8d47-386f-8510-f82bb4e75a3b",
                                "text": "I was roused from my abstraction, and lo and behold! my stockings were all frickled with blood, and God knows how many lives I had to answer for."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0205afb2-4bbf-4234-bb07-1ba40c846c7a",
                                "sense_id": "e8105889-8d47-386f-8510-f82bb4e75a3b",
                                "text": "Striped like a zebra, frickled like a pard, Eyed like a peacock, and all crimson barr'd;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6c6da12-f90f-43de-bfd6-8c49c19a16e0",
                                "sense_id": "e8105889-8d47-386f-8510-f82bb4e75a3b",
                                "text": "Blood frickled from the holes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
